#
# CQ5 fixture — passive capability use versus delegation, discriminated
# structurally with no wrapper class (INHABITED-RUNTIME-STACK.md §CQ5). The
# invocation exercises a PASSIVE capability (a gmeow:usedCapability edge to a
# logic:ActionSchema — an internal sort routine), while a separate gmeow:ToolCall
# DELEGATES to a distinct gmeow:SoftwareAgent (a web-search service) via
# gmeow:usedTool. gmeow:ToolCall / gmeow:usedTool are the agentic slice's terms,
# reused here as instance data (the competency harness runs over the merged
# ontology, so they are defined) — never a TBox dependency of model-serving.

@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/model-serving/> .

# Passive capability: an invocation exercises an internal ActionSchema, no agent.
ex:invSort a gmeow:ModelInvocation ;
    gmeow:usedCapability ex:sortSchema .
ex:sortSchema a logic:ActionSchema .

# Delegation: a tool call hands off to a distinct SoftwareAgent.
ex:tcSearch a gmeow:ToolCall ;
    gmeow:usedTool ex:webSearchAgent .
ex:webSearchAgent a gmeow:SoftwareAgent .
